
# chat-transcript
- label: the /run watch page conversation surface is a Cursor-style chat column (max-width ~760px inside its own overflow-y scroller): the client renders the unified session's events as user bubbles (rounded surface cards), assistant prose through a markdown-lite renderer (paragraphs, inline code chips, bold, bullet/checklist items, fenced code blocks) and expandable "Thought briefly|Ns" markers for thinking blocks — every piece of session text is HTML-escaped before decoration, and the session poll repeats the last etag so an unchanged answer costs no re-render
  id: cuts
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'chat transcript surface' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, implemented]
- label: tool calls render as Cursor-grade cards: a terminal-icon card with a short human title (bash commands are humanized from their first pipeline segment — "Search for <pattern>", "List directory", "Find files" — falling back to the mono command) plus muted binary names ("ls, head"); Read renders as a plain "Read <path>" line; Edit/Write render as file cards with +N/-N line stats derived from diffInfo; two or more consecutive search-type calls (Grep/Glob/search-shaped Bash) group under an "Explored N searches" marker; an error tool_result tints its card and shows an error chip
  id: cutl
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'tool-call presentation' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, implemented]
- label: the transcript carries live/pending/idle/exited states: while state=live the last activity reads as in-progress — trailing tool calls without results get a spinner and shimmer title, and a shimmering "Thinking" (after a user event) or "Planning next moves" (after assistant activity) marker follows the thread; a run with no linked recording shows the pending state ("Waiting for the agent session"); a linked idle TUI (state=idle) shows a non-shimmer Not running marker rather than Planning next moves; and the exited state does one final delayed session poll, stops both pollers, and keeps the full transcript with an "Agent exited" marker
  id: cusp
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'streaming, pending, and exited states' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, implemented]
- label: live appending is smooth and scroll-aware: the chat client polls /api/runs/session at ~1s cadence with the etag flow (unchanged answers skip rendering entirely), swaps the thread only when the rendered HTML actually changed, and sticks the scroller to the bottom on append unless the user has scrolled up (bottom-proximity sampled before every swap)
  id: cusc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'sticks to the bottom|etag flow at ~1s' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, implemented]
- label: the chat transcript is proven live in a real browser: a served run whose stub agent writes growing claude-format JSONL renders the user bubble, thought marker, "Explored 2 searches" grouping, and human tool titles, then renders the appended events (including an Edit file card with +N/-N stats) without a reload while chat polling stays active — and a run that never writes a recording shows the pending state (skips cleanly without playwright/tmux)
  id: cupw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'chat transcript' test/browser/run-watch.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, tests, implemented]
- label: the /run and /run?session= chat documents stay loaded while the watched session grows: both pages set window._stayLoaded so the injected EventSource never location.reload()s the conversation, and they expose window._refreshData that kicks the existing etag session poll (no navigation) when a data-update SSE arrives
  id: cisl
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "stay-loaded live watch|incremental thread apply" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: new transcript content is patched in place: each user, assistant, thought, tool-card, and marker node carries data-role plus a stable data-block-key, applyThreadItems updates or appends by key without assigning chatThread.innerHTML, existing message/tool-card element identity is preserved, and a scroller that is not at the bottom keeps its scrollTop
  id: ciin
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "incremental thread apply|sticks to the bottom" test/browser/run-page.test.js test/browser/chat-thread-apply.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: the /run and /run?session= transcript shows agent turn bodies in full: assistant prose, thinking, and tool_result text appear verbatim in the transcript body (line breaks preserved) without a 500/1000-char cap or a '… [truncated N chars]' marker; tool-card titles may stay short
  id: cuft
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full turn bodies|full-transcript" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= watches a recording that is generating, unmatched tool_use (newest assistant tool_use with no tool_result) can still set growth lastState to running for in-thread tool spinners even if detectLiveSessions reports idle; a completed idle G1 poll whose etag is inside the ~4s quiet window does not — growth lastState follows identity (idle) so containNamedOutput leftover-snaps instead of parking and activityHtml does not emit shimmering Planning next moves; exclusive Stop (#liveTailForm / data-live-tail) follows identity generating (apiLive); a quiet complete recording with no process stays honest idle chrome
  id: cilg
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "growth-driven live tail" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: a completed /run and /run?session= turn keeps assistant prose as the subject: a long tool_result is a first-class named output that follows the complete prose — the in-thread card header names the source (file basename from Read/cat/head/tail, otherwise the human tool title) plus a Lines 1-N range, the full tool_result text lives in pre.chat-tool-body inside that same card (every character kept, no truncation marker, no empty Open-output opener), the card is a line-snapped file object (reserved whole-line reading height plus interior padding, last visible line Range.bottom ≤ card.bottom) rather than a second equal-weight dump, and the card carries chat-output
  id: cuoc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript output card|full-transcript named output body|full turn bodies" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= watches a growing or live recording, the conversation column ends on the exclusive live-ending composer: archive observer chrome (Watching a running session, Open full session view, Export markdown, WATCH-ONLY, continues as a new run) and the composer-status strip live in #archiveEnding and are hidden, and the only footer is #liveTailForm — a slim Send a follow-up composer whose right control is Stop — under Planning/Thinking and empty air; a quiet complete recording with no process restores the archive ending (Watching an idle session) and hides #liveTailForm
  id: cilt
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live tail replaces observer" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: the named /run output body is displayed in the conversation column after the complete assistant prose: containNamedOutput sizes .chat-card.chat-output .chat-tool-body as a line-snapped file object (whole measured line boxes plus interior padding, no fixed 18em cap, no leftover-column overflow:hidden clip), advertised lines stay in the DOM, and the card cuts preferred file-object lines to the leftover above .chat-composer rather than yielding .chat-assistant
  id: cupc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript output card|full-transcript named output body|paints advertised lines" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= watches a growing or live recording, the conversation column ends on exactly one slim generating composer (#liveTailForm): placeholder Send a follow-up, the round right control is Stop (square glyph, not a send arrow), and the archive footer slot (#archiveEnding: composer-status strip, observer card, takeover #continueForm) is hidden — no 34px Generating/Stop strip stacked on a 44px Send-a-follow-up composer, and #continueForm is never data-mode=live-tail
  id: cilc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "exclusive live-ending composer|live tail replaces observer" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: a completed /run and /run?session= turn does not steal conversation-column width for a default-open output pane: #chatOutputPane remains a sibling of .chat-main for click-to-inspect, stays hidden on first idle paint (no data-has-output), and the named output body is in the in-thread card so the column reads prompt then complete answer then named output then follow-up
  id: cuop
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript output pane|full-transcript column width|full-transcript named output body" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: a completed /run and /run?session= turn is framed as a finished undivided answer: first paint of an idle or exited recording scrolls the last user bubble to the top of #chatScroll (frameCompletedTurn, not scrollBottom), so the user prompt and the whole assistant prose are one subject in the default viewport; named output follows that complete prose with its actual body in the card, never a compact opener spliced after the lead paragraph
  id: cuaf
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript finished answer|full-transcript undivided answer" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: a completed /run?session= idle column ends on a slim follow-up composer: .observer-card, .composer-status, and the idle .chat-activity archive line are display:none, #liveTailForm stays hidden, and #continueForm (when present) is a single rounded pill — not a 350px archive/watch/takeover stack
  id: cuas
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript slim answer footer" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: a completed /run and /run?session= turn is one undivided answer above the composer: assistant prose stays a single chat-assistant subject (composeAnswerItems does not split at the first blank line, there is no chat-assistant-more rest node, and no mid-message Open-output chip is inserted into the assistant)
  id: cuua
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript undivided answer" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: the named output follows the complete assistant prose as a first-class card that includes the actual tool_result body in pre.chat-tool-body (every character kept, no truncation marker, not an empty Open-output opener), with a named header (file basename from Read/cat/head/tail or the human tool title, plus a Lines 1-N range)
  id: cuno
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript named output body" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: the default completed-turn paint does not auto-open #chatOutputPane or set data-has-output, so the conversation column keeps its full readable width (chat-col ~760px) and assistant fixture lines are not force-wrapped around a side pane; the pane stays a click-to-inspect sibling, not the default idle layout
  id: cuwp
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript column width" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: the default completed /run and /run?session= turn keeps the named output as a finished file object above the composer: after framing the last user bubble, containNamedOutput leaves .chat-assistant at its natural unclipped height and sizes .chat-card.chat-output .chat-tool-body to leftover room of whole Range-measured lines plus interior padding (last visible line Range.bottom ≤ card.bottom, never a fixed 18em, never leftover-column overflow:hidden that shears a mid-glyph, and never a data-yield max-height on the assistant), every advertised line stays in the DOM, and the card box does not extend under .chat-composer
  id: cucp
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript file object|full-transcript output card|full-transcript named output body" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: the named /run output is a line-snapped file object: containNamedOutput sizes .chat-card.chat-output .chat-tool-body to leftover room of whole measured line boxes plus interior padding (document.createRange on each pre line; last visible line Range.bottom ≤ card.bottom), the card itself is overflow visible so it does not leftover-clip a mid-glyph, advertised tool_result bytes stay in the pre, and a long .chat-assistant stays unclipped (no data-yield, no max-height overflow) so preferred file-object lines are cut first — never a leftover-column overflow:hidden mid-glyph cut and never a fixed 18em cap
  id: cufs
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript file object|full-transcript output card|full-transcript named output body" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: a completed idle /run and /run?session= turn keeps the whole assistant answer on screen: containNamedOutput never sets max-height, overflow, or data-yield on .chat-assistant, so fixture lines L001 through L023 remain in the natural prose flow inside #chatScroll with no inner scroller; the named file object takes only leftover space above .chat-composer and line-snaps its last visible tool line (Range.bottom ≤ card.bottom) by cutting preferred file-object lines first
  id: cual
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "full-transcript leftover|full-transcript file object|full-transcript output card" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, full-transcript, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= watches a growing recording, the conversation column sticks to the live tail (running tool, Planning next moves or Thinking, empty air, slim #liveTailForm) if the user was following the idle leftover-snap frame: follow-tail is sampled before live chrome CSS (chat-activity min-height and chat-col padding-bottom) and before leftover-snap uncap, then #chatScroll.scrollTop is pinned to the tail after that chrome and new activity paint; a user who scrolled up keeps their scrollTop
  id: cist
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live tail sticks|sticks to the bottom|growth-driven live tail" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= watches a growing recording, leftover-snap does not uncap the previous completed file card onto the fold: containNamedOutput parks that completed turn off the live fold (data-contained=parked, height 0, overflow hidden, no 22px data-trail costume and no fixture/Lines header) so the visible column is the last user prompt then this turn's tool cards then Planning/Thinking then natural empty air then #liveTailForm, without a leftover-viewport #chatActivity min-height spacer; advertised assistant and tool_result bytes stay in the parked nodes; an idle completed turn still leftover-snaps the named file object
  id: jtc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live trail not leftover dump|full-transcript leftover|live tail sticks" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= watches a growing recording, the previous completed turn leaves the live fold so this turn's tools sit under the prompt: containNamedOutput parks leftover-snap nodes between the last user bubble and this turn's live work (data-contained=parked, height 0, overflow hidden, no data-trail one-line costume, no named file-object header); this turn's in-progress assistant and tool cards stay visible; #chatActivity is not given a leftover-viewport min-height spacer so Planning/Thinking sits on that trail above natural empty air then #liveTailForm; an idle completed turn still leftover-snaps prompt then whole assistant prose then the named file object
  id: cipa
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live trail not leftover dump|full-transcript leftover|live tail sticks" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= watches a growing recording, the first visible item under the last user prompt is this turn's live work: parkPriorCompletedTurn parks every prior assistant event after the last user (data-contained=parked, height 0) by comparing data-event-index to thisTurnEventIndex — including the last completed assistant that has no following .chat-assistant or .chat-output — so leftover BAR_NEW_TURN_MARKER prose is not first; this turn's running tools and explore marker stay; advertised bytes stay in parked nodes; an idle completed turn still leftover-snaps prompt then whole assistant prose then the named file object
  id: cite
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live trail not leftover dump|this turn live work|full-transcript leftover|live tail sticks" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= watches a growing recording, live trail tool cards use verb-object investigation titles: Bash ls/find/rg cards name the action plus the object of investigation — List workspace root directory for a bare ls (and List <path> directory when a path is present), Find all files under workspace for a bare find (and Find all files under <path> when find has a path), Ripgrep for <pattern> (and in <path> when a search path is present) — plus muted binary names (ls, head); they are not generic binary badges (List directory / Find files)
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "verb-object investigation" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented, spec]
- label: when /run?session= watches a growing recording, the live trail accumulates: later assistant events keep earlier this-turn verb-object cards on the fold (ls | head stays visible when find / rg leftover arrive; those cards are not data-contained=parked) while leftover-snap dump+file and prior completed turns still park to height 0
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live trail accumulates|this turn live work|live trail not leftover dump" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, incremental-live, implemented]
- label: when /run?session= is idle, the slim #continueForm pill matches #liveTailForm chrome so idle-to-live is only the right control: both use placeholder Send a follow-up, the same 22px pill padding/radius, the same neutral border and shadow (not the purple continue-card outline), and #continueForm has margin-top 0 so a hidden observer-card cannot add a 10px gap; continue-as-a-new-run honesty stays on the hidden context chip and the send button title; leftover-snap math, live parking, verb-object titles, stay-loaded patches, and exclusive #liveTailForm are unchanged
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "slim pill chrome|full-transcript slim answer footer|exclusive live-ending composer" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, implemented]
- label: after a /run?session= recording grows and returns to idle, leftover-snap keeps the newest completed turn whole above the slim continue pill: the last .chat-assistant (BAR_NEW_TURN_MARKER after the official measure append) has Range.bottom ≤ .chat-composer top; leftover-snap does not re-frame the first dump or spend leftover on a prior named-output card that sits before that newest turn; first-turn leftover-snap math, live parking, verb-object titles, stay-loaded patches, matching pills, and exclusive #liveTailForm are unchanged
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "leftover-snap after growth|full-transcript leftover|live trail not leftover dump|slim pill chrome" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [chat-ui, ui, idle-live-compose, implemented]
- label: after a /run?session= recording grows and returns to idle, leftover-snap frames the newest completed turn as the reading block: the prior named-output dump is parked off the leftover fold (not a 475px uncap); leftover-snap then frames the last user (or the last .chat-assistant if there is no user) at the top of #chatScroll so that turn's user and assistant own the fold — BAR_NEW_TURN_MARKER after the official measure append is the reading subject, not a 39px caption under the previous dump; the last .chat-assistant Range.bottom stays ≤ .chat-composer top; first-turn leftover-snap (seed only) still leftover-snaps L001–L023; live parking, verb-object titles, stay-loaded patches, matching pills, and exclusive #liveTailForm are unchanged
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "leftover-snap after growth|full-transcript leftover|live trail not leftover dump|slim pill chrome" test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-ui, ui, idle-live-compose, implemented]

# chat-composer
- label: the /run composer is a Cursor-style input card: a rounded bordered surface card holding a context row (an at-sign BUTTON that inserts an at-sign mention into the input and focuses it — a real control, not a decorative circle — plus a chip naming the run cwd's basename with the full path as tooltip), a borderless text input (placeholder "Send a follow-up"), and a bottom control row of caret-marked disclosure chips — the agent chip (infinity glyph + agent name + a visible Cmd/Ctrl-I shortcut, swapped to "Ctrl+I" off-mac), a model chip fed live from the linked session's reported model (hidden until known, dashboard-short name), and the action-labeled "Send key" chip — plus a round arrow send button; no bare run id or unlabeled icons remain in the row; the send button renders accent-colored when text is present and visibly stands down over an empty input (muted circle + faint arrow via data-empty, title admitting the bare-Enter empty-submit), while form submit POSTs {id, text, key:"Enter"} (bare Enter when empty), clears the input, and keeps focus; exited/gone hides the card
  id: cmcd
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'composer input card' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, implemented]
- label: special keys live in a popover, not an always-visible button row: the action-labeled "Send key" chip in the composer's control row (keyboard glyph + "Send key" text + caret, aria-haspopup/aria-expanded) toggles a floating menu listing exactly the six server-allowlisted /api/runs/input keys (Enter, Escape, C-c as "Interrupt", Up, Down, Tab) as labeled rows with kbd glyph chips; the menu closes on outside click, on Escape, when the run-details popover opens, and immediately when a key is sent — the key POSTs {id, key} alone and focus returns to the input
  id: cmky
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'special-keys popover' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, implemented]
- label: run-level status lives in a strip directly above the input card: while live it shows a pulsing green dot + "Running" with right-aligned Stop (kbd ^C — sends key C-c through /api/runs/input to interrupt the agent, never kill) and "Kill run" (POSTs /api/runs/kill) controls rendered as REAL bordered pill buttons (rest-state border + fill, not bare text labels) — the destructive Kill run carries a rest-state red danger tint on text, border, and fill so the interrupt/destroy distinction is visible before reading, and the ^C keycap inside the Stop pill renders as muted glyphs (no nested box); scopes are further explained by labels, hover tooltips (interrupt-and-stay-attached vs end-the-tmux-window), and the run-details popover note; markExited swaps the strip to an orange-dot "Agent exited" and markGone to a red-dot gone reason, both retiring the stop/kill controls and the input card so the strip remains as the run's final status line (the server renders the exited strip directly for an already-exited run)
  id: cmst
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'composer status strip' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, implemented]
- label: the composer is proven in a real browser against a live run: typed text submits via Enter AND via the round send button (data-empty flips as text is typed and clears), the keys popover opens with all six keys and a clicked Enter reaches the agent's tty as a bare Enter while the menu closes and focus returns, the agent chip opens the run-details popover (agent/run-id rows, Stop-vs-Kill-run note, honest "detecting…" model row with the chip hidden while no recording reports a model) mutually exclusive with the keys menu and Escape-closable, a session-writing run unhides the model chip with the shortened session-reported model and links the recording row to /view, and the status strip's Stop control C-c-interrupts the run to the exited state with the strip swapping to "Agent exited" and the card retiring (skips cleanly without playwright/tmux)
  id: cmpw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'composer send paths|composer Stop control|chat transcript renders appended' test/browser/run-watch.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, tests, implemented]
- label: the composer's identity chips are honest disclosure controls, not fake pickers: the agent chip and the model chip both open a run-details popover (mutually exclusive with the keys menu, toggled by click or the chip's visible Cmd/Ctrl-I shortcut, closed by Escape/outside click/run end) listing what the run IS — Agent, Model (full id, "detecting…" until the linked recording reports one), Run id + tmux window, Directory, and Recording (a "view session" link to /view?path=… once linked) — plus a note stating that agent & model are fixed at launch and explaining Stop (^C interrupt) vs Kill run (ends the tmux window, transcript preserved)
  id: cmrd
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run-details popover' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, implemented]
- label: the composer's status strip is state-AWARE while the run is live, never a static label: the strip text is the run's live activity derived client-side from the SAME polled unified session the transcript renders (an unresolved tool call in the newest assistant turn reads as the humanized action — 'Running <cmd>', 'Editing <file>', 'Searching <pattern>' — a session whose last event is a user message or tool result, or whose recording grew within the ~4s quiet window, reads as 'Generating' with a CSS-animated ellipsis; a quiet complete-looking turn falls back to the plain 'Running'), synced on every session poll AND on keystrokes; a run with no linked recording keeps the honest plain 'Running', and the exited/gone strip copy is never touched by the activity sync
  id: cmal
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'in-composer run feedback' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, implemented]
- label: typing mid-generation has a visible, honest consequence — a CLIENT-HELD follow-up queue (there is no server-side queue and the page never pretends one exists): a non-empty submit while the agent is busy is HELD on the page instead of sent, rendered in a queue block above the status strip ('N in queue' collapsible header, hidden while empty) where every row is real — click the text to pull it back into the input for editing, x removes it, 'send now' types it into the agent's terminal immediately — and auto-delivery POSTs items to /api/runs/input IN ORDER only when the run is live and the agent looks ready (activity idle, and the previous delivery either showed up as recording growth or 8s passed), one in flight at a time; the queue persists per-run in sessionStorage, a non-empty queue warns on page close (beforeunload), an EMPTY submit stays an immediate bare Enter (TUI prompts), and when the run ends undelivered rows stay visible under an honest 'nothing was delivered' note instead of vanishing
  id: cmqu
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'follow-up queue' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, implemented]
- label: the round send button is state-aware during generation (data-busy synced onto the composer card): busy + EMPTY input morphs it into a stop control — the arrow icon swaps to a square stop glyph on a high-contrast fill and a click sends key C-c through /api/runs/input WITHOUT submitting the form (preventDefault), title/aria-label saying Stop generating — while busy + text keeps the accent arrow but title/aria-label state the queue consequence and the input placeholder swaps to the queue wording; idle and pending states keep the round arrow with the original send semantics, and continue mode is never touched by the morph (no data-busy, placeholder and titles owned by updateContinueComposer)
  id: cmsm
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'send affordance is state-aware' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, implemented]
- label: the in-composer run feedback is proven in a real browser against a live run: while the stub session holds an unresolved tool call the strip text becomes the humanized live action (not 'Running') with data-busy=true and the empty-input send button morphed to the stop control; typing flips the button back to a queue-labeled send whose Enter HOLDS the message as a visible queue row ('1 in queue', input cleared, nothing typed into the pane) with a second message counting '2 in queue'; x removes a row, clicking a row's text pulls it back into the input, 'send now' types a queued row into the agent's terminal immediately; and once the stub completes its turn and the recording goes quiet the remaining queue auto-delivers in order into the pane and the queue block empties (skips cleanly without playwright/tmux)
  id: cmfw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'in-composer state feedback' test/browser/run-watch.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-composer, ui, tests, implemented]

# app-integration
- label: starting a run is native to the app everywhere — the dashboard header's "+ New run" button opens an in-page launcher modal (agent dropdown listing only detected agents from GET /api/agents, cwd input prefilled from localStorage falling back to the server-embedded defaultCwd, optional prompt textarea) whose Start submit POSTs /api/runs behind an in-flight guard and navigates straight into the run's chat at /run?id=<id> on success; the modal renders non-2xx {error} bodies inline, a no-agents-detected state with disabled controls, and — when mux.available is false — the missing-multiplexer state instead of the form; a ?launch=1 query on the dashboard auto-opens the launcher; the same button + modal are embedded in the /run and /run?session= app header (defaultCwd = the open run's cwd), so a new run starts from any chat without going back to the dashboard
  id: ciln
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'launcher modal' test/browser/launch-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, implemented]
- label: GET /launch is no longer a standalone page — it answers a 302 redirect to /?launch=1 so the dashboard launcher modal is the single launch surface, while the /launch route stays registered so old links keep working
  id: cilr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern '/launch redirects' test/browser/launch-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, implemented]
- label: launched runs are ONE first-class object each on the dashboard — the client polls GET /api/runs (~3s interval plus every fs-watch _refreshData tick, poll signature includes the activity line) and renders every run as a session-styled row PINNED at the top of the main session list (page 1): pulsing running / static exited state badge, agent pill, linked session id once known, cwd basename, launch prompt (tq_prompt served by the API so pending runs have identity), a live "what it's doing now" activity line (server-derived from the linked recording: in-progress tool call or last assistant outcome snippet, with Waiting-for-the-agent-session / Working fallbacks), absorbed model/grade/stats from the linked session row, and a kill/dismiss control POSTing /api/runs/kill; activating the row navigates to the run's chat at /run?id=<id> — the single click target; a session row whose path matches a run's sessionPath is absorbed (dropped from the list and from the Live strip) so a run never appears as two objects, and the Live strip returns to externally-detected live sessions only
  id: cirs
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'run rows|live strip shows only external' test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, implemented]
- label: /run and /view cross-link where they represent the same underlying session — the run page's shell links back to the dashboard (wordmark + session rail "All sessions", with a narrow-viewport "← sessions" text link) and reveals a "view session" link targeting /view?path=<sessionPath> as soon as the session poll reports a linked recording, while /view of a session that is some run's linked recording injects a floating "open chat" chip targeting /run?id=<id> (rendered only while the run's window still exists, with a distinct exited variant)
  id: cixl
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'cross-link' test/browser/run-page.test.js test/browser/launch-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, implemented]
- label: the integrated flow is proven in a real browser — from the dashboard the "+ New run" button opens the launcher modal listing the stub agent, Start lands directly on /run?id=<id> with the chat header showing the run; back on the dashboard the run appears as ONE first-class run row in the main session list (running state badge, launch prompt, activity line, no strip row or chat badge anywhere else) and clicking the row returns to the chat; the row's kill control dismisses the run; with tmux absent the modal shows the missing-multiplexer state; and GET /launch redirects to the dashboard launcher (skips cleanly without playwright/tmux)
  id: cipw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/browser/launch-ui.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, tests, implemented]
- label: entering a run never leaves the app — /run and /run?session= render inside the tracequest shell: the SAME app bar the dashboard renders (shared appTopHtml builder: tracequest wordmark linking home, a "sessions" crumb, the origin-agnostic live counter, and the "+ New run" launcher-modal button; the run page prefills the launcher cwd with the open run's directory), plus a persistent session rail — headed "Sessions", matching its own "All sessions →" foot link — beside the chat pane, client-rendered from GET /api/runs (~3s) and GET /api/sessions?pageSize=30 (every 3rd tick), listing every run (pulsing running dot / check glyph, prompt title, live activity line or agent+project meta, grade chip, short relative time), external live sessions (linking to /run?session=<id>), and recent indexed sessions (linking to /view), with the open chat's row highlighted aria-current
  id: cish
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'app shell' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, implemented]
- label: the chat header repeats the record's dashboard list identity row VERBATIM — the same classes and chips the list card wears: state badge (running/exited, plus idle/gone variants), colored source pill, session id (the server-rendered run id swaps to the linked recording's hash exactly when the list would show it), model chip, project chip (cwd basename, full path only as tooltip and in the run-details popover), grade badge, and the list card's stat chips (duration/chapters/tokens/cost/files/errors/commits) in a second header line — id, model, stats and grade are client-filled from the SAME polled /api/runs + /api/sessions objects the dashboard renders, through the shared sessionStatChipsHtml builder (app-chrome.js), so the two surfaces cannot drift; a relative "started Nm ago" time keeps the ISO stamp in data-started/tooltip; the "← sessions" text link is only the narrow-viewport escape hatch, CSS-hidden whenever the session rail is visible
  id: cihd
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'app shell|identity row|escape hatch' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, implemented]
- label: one noun, one chrome — a live-agent record is a "session" on every surface: the dashboard heading counts sessions, the chat pages' breadcrumb says sessions, the chat rail is headed Sessions above its "All sessions →" foot, and nothing re-badges the record as an "agent" when the chat opens; the dashboard renders the same sticky app-top bar the chat pages use (shared appTopHtml + APP_TOP_CSS from app-chrome.js: wordmark / crumb slot — the dashboard mounts its live "N sessions" count there — / the ● N running counter fed by the one origin-agnostic liveNow definition / "+ New run"), and the identity-row CSS + stat-chip builder are single-sourced in app-chrome.js so the list card and the chat header render one record, not two apps
  id: civn
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'SAME app bar|persistent session rail|identity row verbatim' test/browser/browser-page-build.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, chat-integration, ui, implemented]

